The module compiles cleanly. The implementation uses a 4-bit register that increments on every positive clock edge; since 4-bit arithmetic naturally wraps from 15 back to 0, the counter has a period of 16. The active-high `reset` is synchronous (inside the `posedge clk` block), so it clears the counter to 0 on the next clock edge.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input clk,
    input reset,
    output reg [3:0] q
);

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset)
            q <= 4'd0;
        else
            q <= q + 4'd1;
    end

endmodule
```
